# RestoStack MVP

Goal: safe production multi-tenant app at restostacks.com. Judge every change by deploy safety and speed.

## Before coding

- Read `AGENTS.md`, `docs/AUDIT.md`, `docs/DATA_MODEL.md`, `docs/BUILD_PLAN.md`, `docs/ROUTES.md`.
- Do **not** implement OUT-OF-SCOPE features (POS, Server Pad, orders, revenue metrics, payroll, marketing, loyalty, AI, public marketing site, structured menu items, waitlist SMS, Upgrade to Pro).
- Prefer **delete** over refactor for out-of-scope modules.
- Never commit `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` or Stripe secrets.
- Migrations: one new file per change under `supabase/migrations/`; never edit an applied migration.

## Architecture locks (ADR-001)

- Shared Postgres; isolation via `organization_id` (+ `location_id`) + RLS.
- `organizations` → `locations` → tenant data. No localStorage as tenancy SoT.
- Role-aware RLS: owner / manager / host.
- Public booking only via SECURITY DEFINER RPCs + rate limits.
- Stripe subscription gate: `trialing` | `active` or `/billing/locked`.
- Cross-tenant isolation tests must pass before merge (Phase 0+).

## MVP product surface

Invite→auth→Stripe→onboard · Booking · Dashboard (reservation KPIs only) · Reports · Guests · Host Stand · Menu assets · Settings (incl. Billing).

## Stack

React/TS/Vite/TanStack Router/Tailwind/shadcn · Supabase · GitHub trunk · Vercel deploy (Phase 6). Defaults: CAD, America/Toronto, en-CA.

